			'meta_desc' => 'Google AI Mode is a conversational, AI-first way to search Google. Learn what it is, how it differs from AI Overviews, and what it means for SEO.',
			'excerpt' => 'Google AI Mode is a conversational, AI-first search experience where you ask questions in natural language and Google returns an AI-generated answer you can follow up on, rather than a traditional page of links. It\'s a more immersive version of Google\'s AI search, powered by its Gemini models.',
			'faqs' => array(array('What is Google AI Mode?','Google AI Mode is a conversational, AI-first way to search Google: you ask questions in natural language and get AI-generated answers you can follow up on in a thread, powered by Google\'s Gemini models, rather than a page of links.'),array('How is AI Mode different from AI Overviews?','AI Overviews are AI summary boxes shown at the top of normal search results; AI Mode is a separate, chat-style experience where you can ask follow-up questions. Overviews blend AI into classic search, while AI Mode is a fuller conversational interface.'),array('How do I optimise for Google AI Mode?','Optimise the same way as for other AI search: clear, answer-first content, strong structure and FAQ sections, schema, topical authority, and technical accessibility. Being an authoritative, extractable source is what gets your brand cited in AI Mode answers.'),array('Will AI Mode change SEO?','It reinforces the shift already underway — from ranking links to being cited in AI answers. Core SEO quality still matters, but success increasingly depends on answer-first, extractable, authoritative content that AI can quote. AEO and GEO become central.')),
			'html' => '<nav class="on-this-page" aria-label="On this page"><a href="#what">What it is</a> · <a href="#vs">AI Mode vs AI Overviews</a> · <a href="#brands">What it means for brands</a> · <a href="#faqs">FAQs</a></nav>
<h2 id="what">What is Google AI Mode?</h2>
<p>Google AI Mode is a dedicated, conversational search experience within Google. Instead of typing keywords and scanning links, you ask a question in natural language, get an AI-generated answer, and can ask follow-ups in the same thread — much like chatting with an AI assistant, but grounded in Google\'s search index.</p>
<h2 id="vs">AI Mode vs AI Overviews</h2>
<div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th></th><th>AI Overviews</th><th>AI Mode</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Where</strong></td><td>Top of normal results</td><td>A dedicated conversational experience</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Format</strong></td><td>A summary box above links</td><td>A full AI-first, chat-style answer flow</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Interaction</strong></td><td>One answer per search</td><td>Follow-up questions in a thread</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<p>Both are part of Google\'s shift toward AI answers; AI Overviews blend AI into classic results, while AI Mode is a fuller conversational interface. See <a href="/guides/google-ai-overviews/">AI Overviews explained</a>.</p>
<h2 id="brands">What AI Mode means for brands</h2>
<p>AI Mode reinforces the same lesson as the rest of AI search: visibility increasingly means being cited in a generated answer, not just ranking a link. The optimisation levers are the same — clear, extractable, authoritative content that AI can quote — which makes <a href="/ai-search/answer-engine-optimisation/">AEO</a> and <a href="/ai-search/generative-engine-optimisation/">GEO</a> more important, not less.</p>
<h2>Stay visible as search changes</h2>
<p>Alugence helps brands adapt to AI-first search. Explore <a href="/ai-search/">AI search consultancy</a> or <a href="/contact/">book a call</a>.</p>',
