		array(
			'slug' => 'improve-brand-visibility-ai-search', 'cpt' => 'tf_guide',
			'title' => 'How to improve brand visibility in AI search',
			'meta_title' => 'How to Improve Brand Visibility in AI Search',
			'meta_desc' => 'A practical guide to improving your brand\'s visibility in AI search engines like ChatGPT, Gemini and Perplexity. 10 strategies that work.',
			'excerpt' => 'To improve brand visibility in AI search, make your brand easy for AI engines to understand, extract and trust: keep your entity consistent, add Organization schema, write answer-first content, publish FAQs, allow AI crawlers, and build citations in the sources AI models draw on. Then track your mentions and share of voice across engines.',
			'faqs' => array(array('What strategies improve brand visibility in AI search?','The most effective strategies are: keep your brand entity consistent, add Organization schema and sameAs profiles, write answer-first content with strong FAQs, structure content for extraction, allow AI crawlers, serve content in HTML, build off-site citations, demonstrate expertise, and keep content fresh. Then measure your citations and share of voice.'),array('How do I get my brand mentioned by ChatGPT?','Make your brand easy to understand and trust: a consistent entity, clear schema, answer-first extractable content, permission for AI crawlers, and citations in sources ChatGPT draws on. Building third-party mentions and authority is often the biggest lever. See how to get cited by AI.'),array('How long does it take to improve AI search visibility?','Some improvements show within weeks as engines re-crawl; building durable authority and share of voice usually takes a few months. Because AI search is still new, gains can come faster than in mature SEO markets.'),array('Do backlinks help with AI search visibility?','Indirectly, yes. Links and mentions from trusted sites build the authority and citations that AI models draw on, and often correlate with being referenced in AI answers. But entity clarity and extractable content matter just as much.'),array('Can I improve AI visibility without a big budget?','Yes. Entity consistency, schema, answer-first content and FAQs are largely in your control and cost little but effort. Citation building and cross-engine tracking are where a specialist adds most value once the basics are in place.'),array('Which AI engines should I focus on?','Focus on the engines your customers actually use — commonly ChatGPT, Google AI Overviews and Perplexity, with Gemini and Copilot growing. An audit shows where you currently appear, so you can prioritise the engines that matter most for your audience.'),array('What\'s the single most important thing to fix first?','For most brands it\'s a tie between technical accessibility (making sure AI crawlers can read your content in HTML) and entity consistency (a clear, uniform brand identity with schema). Both are foundational — without them, better content can\'t be found or attributed to you.'),array('How is this different from traditional SEO?','Traditional SEO aims to rank links; improving AI search visibility aims to get your brand mentioned and cited in AI answers. The disciplines overlap — quality and authority help both — but AI visibility adds entity clarity, answer-first content, crawler access and citation building. See AI SEO vs traditional SEO.')),
			'html' => '<nav class="on-this-page" aria-label="On this page"><a href="#why">Why it matters</a> · <a href="#how">How AI decides who to mention</a> · <a href="#strategies">10 strategies</a> · <a href="#plan">A 90-day plan</a> · <a href="#measure">How to measure</a> · <a href="#mistakes">Mistakes to avoid</a> · <a href="#faqs">FAQs</a></nav>
<h2 id="why">Why brand visibility in AI search matters</h2>
<p>When customers ask ChatGPT, Gemini or Perplexity for recommendations, the brands those engines name win attention before a website is ever visited. If your brand isn\'t mentioned, you\'re invisible at the point of decision — even if you rank on page one of Google. Improving AI search visibility means being one of the brands the AI knows, trusts and cites, and it\'s becoming as important as classic rankings. It\'s also, for now, an unusually open opportunity: many AI-search terms are low-competition, so decisive action can build a lead that\'s hard to catch.</p>
<h2 id="how">How AI engines decide which brands to mention</h2>
<p>AI engines mention brands they can <strong>find</strong>, <strong>understand</strong> and <strong>trust</strong>. They find brands whose content is crawlable and served in HTML; they understand brands with a clear, consistent entity and structured content; and they trust brands corroborated by credible third-party sources. Every strategy below targets one of those three: findability, understanding, or trust. Get all three right and you become a natural, repeatable citation.</p>
<h2 id="strategies">10 strategies to improve brand visibility in AI search</h2>
<ol><li><strong>Standardise your brand entity.</strong> Use exactly the same brand name and description everywhere online — models track entity consistency, and inconsistency makes them hesitate to cite you.</li><li><strong>Add Organization schema and sameAs.</strong> Link your site to authoritative profiles (LinkedIn, Crunchbase, Companies House) so models can verify who you are.</li><li><strong>Write answer-first content.</strong> Lead pages and sections with concise, self-contained answers that are easy to quote out of context.</li><li><strong>Publish strong FAQ sections.</strong> FAQs mirror how people query AI — they\'re among the most-cited content formats. Base them on real questions.</li><li><strong>Structure for extraction.</strong> Use question-style headings, short paragraphs, lists and comparison tables that engines can lift cleanly.</li><li><strong>Allow AI crawlers.</strong> Permit GPTBot, PerplexityBot, ClaudeBot, Google-Extended and others in robots.txt, and publish an <a href="/blog/llms-txt-guide/">llms.txt</a> manifest.</li><li><strong>Serve content in HTML.</strong> Many AI crawlers don\'t run JavaScript — ensure key content is in the initial HTML, not rendered client-side.</li><li><strong>Build citations off-site.</strong> Earn mentions in trusted publications, directories and profiles the models draw on. Being <em>talked about</em> by credible sources is a powerful signal.</li><li><strong>Demonstrate expertise (E-E-A-T).</strong> Named authors, credentials, original data and cited sources build the trust models reward.</li><li><strong>Keep content fresh.</strong> Update key pages regularly; retrieval systems favour current sources, so a visible "last updated" date and genuine refreshes help.</li></ol>
<h2 id="plan">A practical 90-day plan</h2>
<p>You don\'t need to do everything at once. A sensible sequence:</p>
<ul><li><strong>Days 1–30 — foundations:</strong> audit current AI visibility; standardise your brand entity; add Organization and FAQ schema; allow AI crawlers and publish llms.txt.</li><li><strong>Days 31–60 — content:</strong> rewrite your most important pages to be answer-first; add FAQ sections based on real questions; fix any JavaScript-only content.</li><li><strong>Days 61–90 — authority and tracking:</strong> begin citation building in trusted sources; set up ongoing visibility tracking; measure share of voice and iterate.</li></ul>
<p>This mirrors how Alugence structures a <a href="/pricing/">GEO/AEO sprint</a> — foundations first, then content, then authority and measurement.</p>
<h2 id="measure">How to measure AI search visibility</h2>
<p>Track how often your brand is mentioned and cited across AI engines for the prompts your customers use, and your share of voice against competitors, over time. This baseline tells you whether your strategies are working. Also monitor AI referral traffic in analytics (from chatgpt.com, perplexity.ai and similar) as a downstream signal. Alugence offers <a href="/ai-search/ai-search-visibility/">AI search visibility tracking and audits</a> to do exactly this — and to benchmark you against rivals.</p>
<h2 id="mistakes">Mistakes that keep brands invisible</h2>
<ul><li><strong>JavaScript-only content</strong> that AI crawlers can\'t read.</li><li><strong>An inconsistent brand entity</strong> across the web, confusing the models.</li><li><strong>Thin or unstructured content</strong> that can\'t be extracted.</li><li><strong>Blocking AI crawlers</strong> in robots.txt, sometimes unintentionally.</li><li><strong>No third-party presence</strong> — a brand nobody credible mentions is hard to trust.</li><li><strong>No measurement</strong>, so you can\'t tell what\'s working or prove progress.</li></ul>
<h2>Grow your presence in AI search</h2>
<p>Alugence helps brands get found by AI. Start with an <a href="/ai-search/ai-search-visibility/">AI search visibility audit</a>, or <a href="/contact/">book a call</a>.</p>',
