			'meta_desc' => 'Perplexity is an AI answer engine that cites its sources. Learn how to optimise your content to get cited by Perplexity and earn AI traffic.',
			'excerpt' => 'Perplexity is an AI answer engine that responds to questions with a concise, generated answer and prominently cites the web sources it used. To be cited by Perplexity, publish clear, well-structured, authoritative content that its crawler (PerplexityBot) can read, and that directly answers the questions your audience asks.',
			'faqs' => array(array('What is Perplexity AI?','Perplexity is an AI answer engine that answers questions by retrieving web information and composing a direct response with visible citations to its sources. It blends search and a large language model, and its prominent citations make it a meaningful referral source.'),array('How do I get cited by Perplexity?','Ensure PerplexityBot can crawl your site and read content in HTML, answer target questions directly and concisely, structure content clearly with FAQs, keep it current, and build topical authority. Perplexity cites relevant, credible, extractable sources.'),array('Does Perplexity send traffic to websites?','Yes. Because Perplexity displays its sources as clickable citations, being cited can drive referral traffic — more visibly than AI tools that don\'t surface sources. Tracking referrals from perplexity.ai shows the impact.'),array('Is optimising for Perplexity different from other AI engines?','The fundamentals are the same as broader LLM optimisation — accessible, extractable, authoritative content — but Perplexity\'s prominent citations make source quality and direct answers especially valuable. Much of the work benefits ChatGPT and Gemini too.')),
			'html' => '<nav class="on-this-page" aria-label="On this page"><a href="#what">What Perplexity is</a> · <a href="#sources">How it chooses sources</a> · <a href="#cited">How to get cited</a> · <a href="#faqs">FAQs</a></nav>
<h2 id="what">What is Perplexity?</h2>
<p>Perplexity is an AI-powered answer engine that combines web search with a large language model. For each query it retrieves current information, composes a direct answer, and lists the sources it drew on as visible citations. Because those citations are front and centre, being cited by Perplexity can send real referral traffic — unlike some AI tools that hide their sources.</p>
<h2 id="sources">How Perplexity chooses sources</h2>
<p>Perplexity favours sources that are relevant, clearly written, current and credible, and that its crawler can access. It tends to cite content that answers the specific question directly and comes from sites with topical authority. Clear structure and a concise, self-contained answer make your content easy for Perplexity to quote.</p>
<h2 id="cited">How to get cited by Perplexity</h2>
<ul><li><strong>Allow PerplexityBot</strong> in robots.txt and serve content in HTML.</li><li><strong>Answer questions directly</strong> — lead with a concise, quotable answer.</li><li><strong>Structure clearly</strong> — headings, short paragraphs, lists, FAQ blocks.</li><li><strong>Keep content current</strong> — Perplexity favours fresh sources.</li><li><strong>Build authority</strong> — depth, credible authorship and citations.</li><li><strong>Publish an <a href="/blog/llms-txt-guide/">llms.txt</a></strong> to guide AI crawlers.</li></ul>
<p>These overlap with <a href="/ai-search/llm-optimisation/">LLM optimisation</a> and <a href="/guides/get-cited-by-ai/">getting cited by AI</a> generally.</p>
<h2>Get cited across AI engines</h2>
<p>Alugence\'s <a href="/ai-search/llm-optimisation/">LLM optimisation</a> gets your brand cited by Perplexity, ChatGPT and more. <a href="/contact/">Book a call</a>.</p>',
